if (2), the ray necessarily enters Oi because we assume interface extractability. This means that, before possibly intersecting any other Oj with j > i, it must exit Oi from a point on the boundary of O , and this leads us back to the previous case;
if (3), before possibly intersecting any other Oj with j > i, the ray must exit Oi, reducing to one of the previous two cases.
